<item>
            <title>[JGVT-2276] Reports_Audit Trail: System Audit Trail - Admin Interface - Filter</title>
                <link>https://jira.jnj.com/browse/JGVT-2276</link>
                <project id="46901" key="JGVT">TDS - Revvity Signals ELN</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;As an administrator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
I want to be able to interact with the system audit trail in the user interface in a flexible and efficient way so that I can review GxP audit information in a targeted and structured manner.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All available audit trail data must be put in 1 table&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I want to be able to sort records by column, navigate large result sets through paging and page-size controls, and quickly filter the visible rows to focus on the subset relevant to my review. The approach should be generic and reusable so that the same interaction pattern can be applied to other tabular datasets as well.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I also want the solution to be easy to extend with export capabilities, including clear feedback when an export is based on a filtered subset of records. In addition, the package should support future enhancement with an advanced query builder for more complex searches and combinations of criteria.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;Design notes&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;part 1: back end&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Current endpoint shall provide the entire current dataset as 1 table (besides xls) as flat file.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt; there are multiple subsets for: Notebook, Attributes, ADO, External Action, Data Source, System Group, Materials Definition, Roles, SO Properties, Security Policy, Templates, System Settings, Global Numbering, Users.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt; for these sections (aka tabs in Excel output) ADO, External Action, Data Source, Materials Definition, Roles, SO Properties, Security Policy and Global Numbering introduce a column &quot;Old Value&quot; with fixed value &quot;N/A&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;part 2: front end&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Extend the current entry page &lt;a href=&quot;https://dev.ui.eln-integrations.im.jnj.com/signals-system-audit-trail-download.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://dev.ui.eln-integrations.im.jnj.com/signals-system-audit-trail-download.html&lt;/a&gt; (dev varies depending environment)&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;with a button for browsing SAT audit trail -&amp;gt; &quot;Browse Audit Trail&quot;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/attachment/7155387/7155387_image-2026-08-12-13-28-14-983.png&quot; height=&quot;377&quot; width=&quot;381&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Click on &quot;Browse Audit Trail&quot; opens in a new webpage:&lt;br/&gt;
If no audit trail data -&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/attachment/7156836/7156836_image-2026-08-12-14-57-42-600.png&quot; height=&quot;139&quot; width=&quot;1027&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
With audit trail data-&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/attachment/7155354/7155354_image-2026-08-12-12-59-03-343.png&quot; height=&quot;311&quot; width=&quot;1015&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/attachment/7156845/7156845_image-2026-08-12-15-03-38-040.png&quot; height=&quot;108&quot; width=&quot;563&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/attachment/7155391/7155391_image-2026-08-12-13-31-44-756.png&quot; height=&quot;387&quot; width=&quot;898&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The solution shall be implemented as a plain JavaScript client-side component using standard HTML and JavaScript, with DataTables as the primary interactive table library. The implementation shall support a generic table initialization pattern that can be applied to any HTML table and shall not depend on a framework-specific architecture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Get the data from the above endpoint with built-in feature (AJAX).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The component shall provide built-in column sorting, global search, paging, and configurable page-size controls. Filtering shall be implemented at the row level so that users can narrow the visible dataset based on current values in the table. The solution shall support a reusable configuration model so that the same component can be applied to audit trails and other tabular views with minimal adaptation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Export functionality shall be designed as an extension point that can be enabled easily. When a user exports data after applying filters or narrowing the visible rows, the system shall display a clear message indicating that the export contains the currently displayed subset of records. The implementation shall allow future addition of advanced query builder capabilities through a modular configuration layer for multi-condition filtering and more complex search logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;Test notes&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
